INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "I find myself in a new and unfamiliar place, surrounded by rolling hills and sparse woodlands. The air feels cool against my skin, and the sun warms me gently as a soft breeze brushes past. I can hear the faint trickle of water nearby, which I assume is the small stream described in my surroundings. My body feels a bit hungry and thirsty, and my energy is not at its peak, but I don’t feel immediate danger. I notice my hunger is more pressing than my thirst, as my stomach grumbles, and I feel a slight weakness from it. My first instinct is to address this need.    I decide to search for food among the scattered wild fruits mentioned in the environment. I will walk carefully through the hills, observing my surroundings for any colorful or distinct shapes that might be fruits hanging from low branches or shrubs. I don’t know what these fruits look like or if they are safe to eat, but my hunger pushes me to try. I will pick a small amount at first and examine them closely—smelling them and touching them to see if they feel soft or ripe. If they seem edible based on my limited judgment, I will taste a tiny bit and wait to see if my body reacts poorly before eating more.    At the same time, I keep an eye on the stream’s location since water is also a concern, though less urgent right now. If I feel too tired or notice any wildlife that makes me uneasy, especially the medium-sized predators mentioned, I will retreat to a natural overhang or dense shrubs for cover. My reasoning for this plan is simple: I need to sustain myself to keep my energy up, and food seems like the most immediate way to do that. I also want to stay safe, so I’ll remain cautious and avoid taking unnecessary risks with unknown wildlife.    After this initial action, I have learned a few things from my experience today:    1. Hunger and thirst are physical needs that can affect how I feel and my energy levels. Addressing them is important for my well-being.    2. The environment provides resources like fruits and water, but I must be careful as I don’t know if they are safe or how to use them properly yet.    3. Wildlife, especially predators, could be a threat, so I need to stay alert and have a plan to hide or protect myself if needed.    4. Observing and testing things slowly, like tasting a small bit of fruit, might help me avoid harm while learning what is safe."}
