INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "I wake up to the warmth of the sun on my skin and the sound of a nearby stream. My body feels a bit stiff, and there's a mild ache from what I assume are small injuries, though I’m not entirely sure how I got them. My stomach grumbles slightly, and I feel a dryness in my throat, indicating I need food and water soon. My energy feels low, like I haven't fully recovered from whatever I did before this moment. Looking around, I see rolling hills turning into thicker woods, with a stream not too far off. I notice some fruits on low bushes, though there aren't many left, and I can hear small animals scurrying nearby. The stream might have fish, but I’m not sure how to catch them yet. There are also places that could shelter me—overhangs in the hills and dense shrubs or trees. I don’t feel immediate danger, but I sense that something bigger might be watching from a distance, and that makes me uneasy.\n\nMy first thought is to address my thirst since water seems close and vital. I decide to walk to the stream to drink and maybe wash myself, hoping the water is safe. I’m cautious as I move, keeping an eye out for any sudden movements from animals or anything that feels off. After drinking, I plan to pick whatever fruits are left on the bushes nearby to ease my hunger, even if it’s not much. I don’t know how to hunt or fish yet, so I’ll avoid the rodents and fish for now. I also want to find a safe spot under one of the overhangs in the hills to rest and observe my surroundings more, as my energy is low, and I don’t feel ready to explore too far into the woods where predators might lurk. I choose the overhang because it feels more protective than just shrubs or trees.\n\nI’m making these decisions because my body’s needs—water, food, rest—feel urgent, and I don’t understand enough about this place to take risks. I’m wary of the wildlife, especially after noticing how some animals seem cautious around me, which makes me think I’ve disturbed them before, even if I can’t remember it. I’m also reflecting on how little I know; everything feels new and overwhelming, but I’m trying to focus on what seems safest and most immediate. I hope to learn more by watching and listening as I rest under the overhang—maybe I’ll figure out patterns in the animals’ behavior or spot dangers I can’t see yet."}
