ging experience: minimizing disturbance to the environment is crucial to avoid attracting predators. The stream area, with its muddied banks from repeated use, is clearly a hotspot for activity, and staying there increases the risk of an encounter. Moving to the woodlands might offer a fresh start in a less disturbed area, and the dense cover could help me stay hidden. I feel a mix of caution and determination\u2014I\u2019m uneasy about the predators, but I\u2019m relieved to take proactive steps to protect myself. I\u2019ll reflect on this experience afterward to see if relocating proves effective in reducing danger.",
