drives me to plan carefully for future needs like food sourcing once energy improves.",      "lesson_learned": "In survival, prioritizing rest and shelter is critical when energy and health are severely compromised, as it lays the foundation for addressing other needs like hunger later with greater strength. Stealth and minimal activity remain essential to reduce environmental disturbance and the risk of predator encounters. I must continue to balance immediate recovery with long-term safety by limiting activity in one area, varying my interactions with the environment, and staying alert for signs of escalating danger. This reinforces past lessons about sustainable interaction with my surroundings and the importance of pacing myself according to my physical limits.",      "timestamp": "First shelter construction near ravine in dense woodlands with focus on recovery and stealth, updated after prioritizing rest in the shelter."    }  }}
