INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "Given my current state and the environment around me, I’ve decided to focus on addressing my high hunger level (8) by cautiously foraging for food in the unexplored areas beyond the ravine, where resources are likely to be more abundant. My energy is low (3), and my overall health is moderate (5), so I must move carefully to avoid exhausting myself or worsening my condition. I’ll use my Basic Stealth Movement skill to minimize disturbance to the wary wildlife and reduce the risk of attracting predators, as I’ve learned from past experiences that repeated activity in one area can escalate danger. I’ll also apply caution by testing any new plants or insects for safety before consuming them, as I’ve noted the risks of potential poisoning from unknown resources in my diary.\n\nMy reasoning for this action is driven by the urgent need to address hunger, which is critical for maintaining my energy and health in this survival situation. The original clearing’s food resources are nearly depleted, as observed in the environment update and reinforced by my past foraging notes, which highlight the importance of sustainability and exploring new terrain when resources dwindle. The unexplored woodlands beyond the ravine offer a potential for better yield, as noted in the terrain description, making it a necessary risk to take despite my low energy. I’m also mindful of the low to moderate danger level and my high luck factor (8), which provides some reassurance, but I won’t rely on it entirely—my past moral reflections remind me to balance immediate needs with long-term safety.\n\nI’ll start by moving slowly from my hidden shelter near the ravine, using the thick tree cover for concealment, and head toward the denser, unexplored areas. I’ll keep my movements deliberate and quiet, watching for signs of small rodents or birds that could be a food source, as well as edible plants or insects. My diary lessons on minimizing environmental disturbance guide me to avoid over-foraging in one spot, so I’ll spread out my search and take only what I need for now. I’m also aware of the trickle of water nearby, which I can return to if thirst becomes an issue, though it’s not my priority at this moment (thirst at 4).\n\nI’m reflecting on the potential consequences of this decision: venturing into unexplored terrain could expose me to new risks, such as hidden predators or unsafe resources, especially with my slight injuries (injury level 2) and compromised immunity (illness at 4). However, staying in the depleted clearing guarantees hunger will worsen, which could further drain my energy and make me more vulnerable. My past emotional responses, like regret for not seeking alternatives sooner, push me to act proactively now. I’m also considering the impact on wildlife—my diary notes show that repeated activity increases wariness and predator curiosity, so I’ll aim to leave as little trace as possible in this new area.\n\nAfter foraging, I plan to return to my secure shelter near the ravine to rest and conserve energy, ensuring I don’t overexert myself. If I find food, I’ll assess its safety by tasting small amounts, as I’ve done before, and monitor my body for any adverse reactions. If I sense any increase in danger, such as fresh predator tracks, I’ll prioritize safety and retreat immediately, as my conscience notes emphasize the importance of weighing survival needs against risks.\n\nLessons I hope to learn from this experience include a better understanding of the resources available beyond the ravine and how to forage sustainably in denser terrain. I also aim to refine my stealth skills further by observing how wildlife reacts to my presence in this new area. My goal is to balance my immediate need for food with the long-term need to avoid overexposure and maintain safety, building on the lessons from my diary about varying locations and minimizing my footprint."}
