                "timestamp": "First shelter construction near ravine in dense woodlands with focus on recovery and stealth, updated after prioritizing rest in the shelter."
            },
            "note_8": {
                "context": "Foraging in unexplored dense woodlands beyond the ravine due to high hunger and low energy. Subsequent foraging near the ravine to address persistent hunger and thirst.",
                "action": "Cautiously foraged for food in new terrain using Basic Stealth Movement to minimize disturbance to wildlife and reduce predator risk, testing plants and insects for safety before consumption. Later, addressed thirst by drinking from the ravine trickle and foraged briefly nearby for edible plants and insects.",
                "outcome": "Successfully foraged a moderate yield of edible plants and small rodents with minimal immediate risk due to high luck factor; wildlife wariness heightened due to presence in previously undisturbed areas and recent activity near the ravine; predator alertness slightly increased but remains moderate with dense cover and stealth. Thirst partially addressed by drinking from the ravine, though repeated activity has further depleted nearby food resources and increased environmental disturbance.",
